WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.689
There was once a rich country called Staten where the people had everything imaginable.

2
00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:14.031
Many great cities were built, and new businesses were started to make useful products.

3
00:00:14.032 --> 00:00:17.869
But the Emperor of Staten was very greedy.

4
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:22.592
He believed that Statens could have anything they wanted.

5
00:00:22.593 --> 00:00:28.361
So the emperor put together the greatest army that had ever been formed.

6
00:00:28.362 --> 00:00:34.343
He filled his army with the most intelligent and hardworking people in Staten.

7
00:00:34.344 --> 00:00:43.916
His generals trained their troops very well, and the army built very powerful weapons that no other country could ever defeat.

8
00:00:43.917 --> 00:00:54.534
One day a report came to the emperor that the most valuable treasure in the world was hiding in a far-off land called Greenport.

9
00:00:54.535 --> 00:01:01.142
The emperor summoned his generals and ordered them to bring him the secret treasure.

10
00:01:01.143 --> 00:01:04.315
The generals were happy to help the emperor.

11
00:01:04.316 --> 00:01:08.479
They had heard that Greenport was very small and weak.

12
00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:14.524
Greenport's army was not very well-trained and its leaders were simple monks.

13
00:01:14.525 --> 00:01:21.354
Instead of building great cities, the leaders of Greenport spent their days praying.

14
00:01:21.355 --> 00:01:27.047
So one general and a small army went to Greenport to get the treasure.

15
00:01:27.048 --> 00:01:32.449
When they arrived, the Great Monk of Greenport came out to greet them.

16
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:37.460
The general demanded that the Great Monk give him the secret treasure.

17
00:01:37.461 --> 00:01:42.739
"I cannot give it to you," said the monk, "but I can share it with you.

18
00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:44.999
I hope that will please you."

19
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.532
The general did not even reply to the monk.

20
00:01:48.533 --> 00:01:53.081
He called his men to attack Greenport and find the treasure.

21
00:01:53.082 --> 00:01:58.355
So the Great Monk and all the other monks of Greenport began to pray.

22
00:01:58.356 --> 00:02:04.523
After a fierce battle, many Statens and Greenporters were dead.

23
00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:11.847
Instead of fighting more, the general sailed back to Staten to tell the emperor what had happened.

24
00:02:11.848 --> 00:02:17.986
The emperor was angry. How could his army be defeated by praying monks?

25
00:02:17.987 --> 00:02:24.570
But he was determined to get the treasure, and he decided to send a larger army.

26
00:02:24.571 --> 00:02:30.908
When the new army arrived, it demanded that the monk give the treasure to the army.

27
00:02:30.909 --> 00:02:40.248
But the monk shed a small tear and spoke the same words, "I cannot give it to you, but I can share it with you.

28
00:02:40.249 --> 00:02:42.664
I hope that will please you."

29
00:02:42.665 --> 00:02:49.143
Once again the general called his men to attack Greenport and find the treasure.

30
00:02:49.144 --> 00:02:53.932
But once again the monks prayed and the Statens failed.

31
00:02:53.933 --> 00:02:59.446
The general had to go back to the emperor and tell him what had happened.

32
00:02:59.447 --> 00:03:01.941
The emperor was furious.

33
00:03:01.942 --> 00:03:07.193
This time he would send a huge army to fight the monks of Greenport.

34
00:03:07.194 --> 00:03:14.387
He would find the secret treasure and kill all the praying monks, even the Great Monk.

35
00:03:14.388 --> 00:03:17.729
The emperor gathered his best generals.

36
00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:23.743
Together they formed the largest and greatest army that had ever been organized.

37
00:03:23.744 --> 00:03:30.468
They sailed up to Greenport and demanded that the monk give them the secret treasure.

38
00:03:30.469 --> 00:03:37.905
The monk cried out in a loud voice, "I cannot give it to you, but I can share it with you.

39
00:03:37.906 --> 00:03:43.462
I hope that will please you." The Staten army attacked once again.

40
00:03:43.463 --> 00:03:49.930
This time no prayer from the monks could save the people of Greenport.

41
00:03:49.931 --> 00:03:57.270
The Statens fought until they had killed everyone, including the Great Monk of Greenport.

42
00:03:57.271 --> 00:04:00.895
Then they began searching for the secret treasure.

43
00:04:00.896 --> 00:04:09.908
They quickly found a large, beautiful gold box in the center of the room where the monks used to pray.

44
00:04:09.909 --> 00:04:17.073
One of the Staten generals broke open the box and stared with disbelief at the secret treasure.

45
00:04:17.074 --> 00:04:27.270
The secret treasure was a note written on a beautiful scroll that read: "Love all people, and share whatever you have.

46
00:04:27.271 --> 00:04:30.153
This is the greatest treasure."

